# ADR-005: Decision to Run Container on ECS
## Status: Accepted (Date: 2026-10-20)
## Context
The Astro application is packaged as a Docker container, but running it on
developers' local devices does not make the server available to site visitors.
The existing S3 and CloudFront setup can serve static files but cannot run the
server-rendered application. Publishing the container image to Amazon ECR
stores it, but a separate compute service is needed to run it.

## Decision
Run the application container as an Amazon ECS service using AWS Fargate.
Store the image in Amazon ECR and expose the service through an Application
Load Balancer. Provision the service and its supporting infrastructure with
AWS CDK.

## Consequences
- Positive: Fargate runs the container without requiring us to manage the
  underlying EC2 instances.
- Negative: The Fargate service and Application Load Balancer incur ongoing
  AWS charges.